Create Package.swift:
```swift
// swift-tools-version: 6.0
import PackageDescription
let package = Package(
    name: "TrailTests",
    targets: [
        .target(name: "TrailKit"),
        .testTarget(name: "TrailKitTests", dependencies: ["TrailKit"])
    ]
)
```
.testTarget names the test code and says it needs TrailKit. Put the files at the exact paths shown in the next steps, inside this package folder.

Create Tests/TrailKitTests/TrailTests.swift:
```swift
import Testing
import TrailKit
@Test func prefixesPlace() {
    #expect(routeName("Cove") == "Route:Cove")
    #expect(routeName("") == "Route:")
}
```
@Test marks prefixesPlace as a test for the runner to find. #expect checks that an expression is true. This test checks both a named place and empty text.
